---js
{
  layout: "layouts/base.webc",
  meta: {
    title: "The DynamoDB conformance suite",
    description: "How faithfully does each DynamoDB emulator match the real thing? An independent conformance suite, scored against live AWS DynamoDB and tracked run over run.",
  },
  // The home page renders the latest run's standings, so its freshness tracks
  // the data, not this file's git date. Keeps the sitemap <lastmod> honest.
  eleventyComputed: {
    lastmod: (data) => data.conformance?.latest?.date,
  },
}
---

<section class="home-intro max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6">
  <div class="hero-copy">
    <p class="eyebrow">Independent DynamoDB conformance tests</p>
    <h1>How close is <span>compatible?</span></h1>
    <p class="hero-description">DynamoDB emulators, put to the test. Explore what matches real AWS, what diverges, and what matters for your application.</p>
    <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button-primary" href="/targets">Explore emulators <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="button-secondary" href="/methodology">How we measure <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
  </div>

</section>


<standings-table></standings-table>

<section class="home-outro max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 pb-20">
  <div>
    <p class="eyebrow">Explore the results</p>
    <h2>See which operations match.</h2>
    <p>Browse operation support, failing tests, and regional comparisons.</p>
  </div>
  <a href="/targets" class="button-secondary">Browse emulator support <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
</section>
